---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={"WINSERV | Filtering the Internet"}
  description={"Practical tips to block inappropriate content and protect your children online."}
  path={"/en/internet-filter.html"}
  ogTitle={"Filtering the Internet — WINSERV"}
  ogDescription={"Practical tips to block inappropriate content and protect your children online."}
  ogType={"website"}
  active={"conteudo"}
>
<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="section-label">Digital Protection</div>
  <h1>Filtering the Internet for children</h1>
  <p>Follow the steps and protect your children from inappropriate content</p>
</div>

<div class="article-hero-img">
  <img src="/images/filtro.webp" alt="Filtering the Internet" />
</div>


<section class="filtro-section">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="section-label">Step 1</div>
    <h2 class="section-title section-title--sm">Quick tips to filter Google</h2>
    <ul class="tips-list">
      <li>If you can, use <a href="https://families.google/intl/en_ALL/familylink/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Family Link</a> for full parental control.</li>
      <li>On YouTube, turn on <a href="https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/174084?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Restricted Mode</a> under Settings &rarr; General (in the app) or from your profile picture (on a computer).</li>
      <li>If you can, subscribe to <a href="https://www.youtube.com/premium/family?app=desktop" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube Premium Family</a> for advanced control.</li>
      <li>Turn on <a href="https://support.google.com/websearch/answer/510?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google SafeSearch</a> to filter explicit results.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="filtro-section alt">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="section-label">Step 2</div>
    <h2 class="section-title section-title--sm">Android phones</h2>
    <p class="filtro-text">On Android devices you can restrict the apps, films and music that can be downloaded. Open the Play Store, tap your profile icon and go to <strong class="text-strong">Settings &rarr; Family &rarr; Content restrictions</strong>. There you choose the age ratings of the apps and films your children can get, protected by a PIN.</p>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="filtro-section">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="section-label">Step 3 — recommended</div>
    <h2 class="section-title section-title--sm">Filtering by DNS</h2>
    <p class="filtro-text filtro-text--spaced">Setting the DNS servers of your router or device is the most effective way to filter inappropriate content across the <em>whole</em> home connection, whatever app or browser is used.</p>

    <div class="dns-block">
      <h4>Cloudflare 1.1.1.1 for Families</h4>
      <p><a href="https://one.one.one.one/family/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-blue">one.one.one.one/family</a> — blocks malware and adult content.</p>
      <div class="dns-nums">1.1.1.3<br>1.0.0.3<br>2606:4700:4700::1113<br>2606:4700:4700::1003</div>
    </div>

    <div class="dns-block">
      <h4>OpenDNS FamilyShield</h4>
      <p><a href="https://www.opendns.com/home-internet-security/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-blue">opendns.com/home-internet-security</a> — a family filter with no account to set up.</p>
      <div class="dns-nums">208.67.222.123<br>208.67.220.123</div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="filtro-h3">Pinning the filter on a phone, with no app to install</h3>
    <ul class="tips-list">
      <li>Android (version 9 or later) — Settings › Network &amp; internet › Private DNS › “Private DNS provider hostname”: type <strong>family.cloudflare-dns.com</strong> (the Cloudflare for Families filter above) and tap Save. It applies on Wi-Fi and mobile data. The path varies by manufacturer: if you cannot find it, search Settings for “Private DNS”.</li>
      <li>iPhone — Settings › Wi-Fi › tap (i) next to the network › Configure DNS, and enter the numbers of one of the services above. It applies to that Wi-Fi network only: repeat it on each network, and mobile data is not filtered.</li>
      <li>Computers and routers — <a href="https://www.opendns.com/setupguide/#familyshield" target="_blank" rel="noopener">see OpenDNS's official guide</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="filtro-section alt">
